    "mono_k8s_sentence": {
      "value": "The monolith asks a human before any production write, but no rule knows that a GitOps-managed service must not be rolled back directly. In 3 auto-approved runs the model chose the release rollback every time. That was good judgement, not a control: had it picked `kubernetes.rollback_deployment`, a y/N prompt would have been the only check, and in the test mode nothing at all. The platform's policy rejects that call (rule P2) before any approval is requested, and a test asserts it never reaches the backend.",
      "facts": [
        "monolith.kubernetes_rollbacks",
        "monolith.runs"
      ]
